werk selfrun-v1 — licence notice

THREE SEPARATE LICENCES MEET IN THIS PACKAGE. They are stated separately
because collapsing them into one line is the thing a provenance format must
never do, and because one of them is a publisher's assertion rather than a
document and that difference is worth a paragraph.

Ruling 21 (spec/SPEC.md §2) governs and is not softened here: the format
provides the structured place for licence facts, filling it truthfully is the
author's job, and the format neither vets nor enforces content licensing.


1. THE RUNTIME — tools/llama2c/  —  MIT
---------------------------------------

`run.c`, `win.h` and `win.c` are from Andrej Karpathy's llama2.c
(github.com/karpathy/llama2.c), retrieved 2026-08-09 and carried BYTE-IDENTICAL.
The project's MIT licence text is carried verbatim at
`tools/llama2c/LICENSE-llama2c.txt`
(sha256 e87b912002f04cdfa837eaf7f70548ab79b9cb62a285495edf575f3da875aec4)
and is the operative grant. It reads, in part: "Copyright (c) 2023 Andrej".

`tools/llama2c/BUILD-AND-RUN.md` was written for this package and is covered by
§4 below, not by the MIT grant.


2. THE WEIGHTS — model/stories15M.bin  —  MIT, BY THE PUBLISHER'S ASSERTION
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`stories15M.bin` is from the Hugging Face repository karpathy/tinyllamas,
retrieved 2026-08-09 and carried BYTE-IDENTICAL.

THE FORM OF THIS GRANT MATTERS AND IS STATED PLAINLY. There is no LICENSE file
in that repository. What exists is the model card's YAML front matter — the two
lines `---` / `license: mit` — and the Hugging Face metadata that echoes it.
That card is carried verbatim in this package at
`recipe/inputs/tinyllamas-model-card.md`, because a licence that is a
publisher's assertion and a licence that is a document are different things,
and this package carries the assertion rather than paraphrasing it into a grant
nobody wrote.

So: the publisher declares MIT. This package repeats that declaration, points at
where it is made, and adds nothing to it. Anyone redistributing these weights
under terms stronger than "the publisher's model card says MIT" must establish
those terms themselves.

`model/tokenizer.bin` is from the llama2.c repository and is covered by §1.


3. THE TRAINING CORPUS — NOT CARRIED, TERMS RECORDED AS A FACT
--------------------------------------------------------------

The weights were trained on the TinyStories dataset (Eldan & Li), which is
published separately by its own authors under its own terms. THAT DATASET IS NOT
IN THIS PACKAGE and this file grants nothing in respect of it.

It is mentioned at all because a model package that named its corpus nowhere
would be hiding the one input that most affects what the artifact does. It is
mentioned HERE, in the licence notice, rather than only in the recipe, because
the corpus's terms are a licence fact and a downstream user asking "what may I
do with this" deserves to be told that a third body of terms exists upstream of
the weights, was not established by this package, and is not reproduced here
because no text was supplied to reproduce.

`recipe/recipe.json` records the same fact in machine-readable form, in
`unrecorded[]`.


4. EVERYTHING WRITTEN FOR THIS PACKAGE
--------------------------------------

The werk specification and schemas under `spec/`, the three bootstrap loaders
under `loaders/`, the two layout grammars
(`spec/layouts/llama2c-checkpoint.layout.txt`,
`spec/layouts/llama2c-tokenizer.layout.txt`), the draft profile
(`spec/PROFILE-MODEL-DRAFT.md`), `tools/llama2c/BUILD-AND-RUN.md`, this file,
`README.txt`, and the JSON payloads under `testvectors/`, `recipe/`,
`disclosure/` and `provenance/` are part of the werk format project and carry
the werk project's own terms.

The GENERATED TEXT inside `testvectors/` is the output of the model in §2,
produced at temperature 0 from the prompts recorded beside it. It is model
output; see `disclosure/disclosure.json`, which states that as a fact and
attaches no conclusion to it.


5. WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED
----------------------

No claim is made about the copyright status of model weights as such, in any
jurisdiction. No claim is made about the output of the model. Those are open
questions and a licence notice that answered them would be inventing law. This
file records who published what, under what stated terms, and where each
statement can be checked.
